 levels, it would be great to be able to suppress this issue on individual properties:\r\n```php\r\nclass A {\r\n  /**\r\n   * @var string\r\n   * @psalm-suppress PropertyNotSetInConstructor\r\n   */\r\n  private $b;\r\n  \r\n  public function __construct() {}\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nMy specific use-case for this is auto-populated properties of Doctrine objects (kinda like ORM behaviours).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/409/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/409/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]